# Tangerine Compiler — Semantic Snapshot Builder (audit §30)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# The analysis slice that fills the semantic_model.tg records from the
# FINALIZED semantic state of one compilation — never from source scanning:
# the inputs are the finalized checker env (TypeEnv), the finalized typed
# program (TypedProgram — the typed def tables, the resolver snapshots, the
# merged program) and the VERIFIED MIR program (the instance the compile
# phases guard with verify_mir / the completeness oracle — see the
# TANGERINE_SNAPSHOT hook in compiler_core.tg's compile_file_core).
#
# TABLE ANCHORS (what each table is populated from):
#   symbols    — the resolver's REGISTRATION tables of the typed program
#                (ResolvedNames.module_symbols — the "path::name" -> DefId
#                registry — plus def_kinds), one row per registered def.
#                Pub marking / generic-ness / contracts come from a
#                deterministic ITEM WALK over the merged program (the same
#                shape the resolver's symbol-table construction uses:
#                top-level items in Program.items order, inline-module
#                recursion appending module segments; first-wins like the
#                resolver). A declaration that lost a first-wins
#                registration has no registry identity and never appears.
#   types      — the CANONICAL TYPE TABLES of the finalized env
#                (TypeEnv.type_list via the TypeId-to-declaration
#                association): nominal TypeDefKind Struct / Enum / Trait
#                declarations only (aliases and primitive/opaque rows are
#                excluded — the SemanticTypeKind vocabulary has no row for
#                them; aliases still ride the symbols table).
#   calls      — the verified MIR's call terminators of def-keyed
#                functions: the callee is the terminator's MirFnItem
#                INSTANCE payload (the solved InstanceId the checker
#                stamped — its DefId); name-only constants resolve through
#                the def-keyed emission-name index (built once in the
#                context — NEVER a per-row function scan); the synthesized
#                intrinsic-name family classifies as Intrinsic edges.
#                Indirect VALUE calls have no statically-known declaration:
#                they are recorded as explicit indirect_calls rows below
#                (item 13) and fail closed (unknown) in the effects table.
#   indirect_calls — one row per indirect call site of the verified MIR
#                (a call whose callee is not statically known): caller row
#                key text + the §33 "<caller key>#B<block>#T" site text +
#                the canonical callee-surface text + the known candidate
#                set. The snapshot's call builder carries NO points-to
#                information, so every row is emitted with an EMPTY
#                candidate set and completeness "Unknown" (the audit's
#                conservative default — a change report must treat the
#                caller of an Unknown row as reachable from anything).
#   effects    — the §11 EffectSummary records computed per function over
#                the verified MIR (the mir.tg §11 machinery reused
#                verbatim — mir_effect_scan_function), propagated to the
#                transitive fixed point over the whole lowered program
#                (the check_effect_class_annotations_mir union shape over
#                every function, not only the claimed roots). Rows exist
#                for the DEF-KEYED functions only (the summaries of the
#                synthesized bodies ride their mir_functions rows).
#   capabilities — Requires edges = the §11 final summary's capability set
#                (the CapabilityId domain). Provides edges are EMPTY: the
#                MIR summaries model only what a body requires.
#   ownership  — MIR move/consume/drop sites (MirMovePlace / MirConsume
#                operands, MirDeinit terminators, the move/consume write
#                destinations of MirAssign, MirRef sites) as per-place
#                OwnershipFact rows: Sink = moved/consumed/dropped,
#                Set = a move/consume write destination, Inout = a
#                mutable-reference creation. Shared READ facts (Let) are
#                elided: reads outnumber every other class by an order of
#                magnitude and add no delta signal (documented).
#   contracts  — the DEF TABLES: the ContractClause records on the
#                function/method declarations of the typed item walk,
#                lowered to their CANONICAL FORM (item 11): each row
#                carries its StableContractId (the stable_ids row key
#                "<fn key>|Pre|Post|Invariant|<canonical text>"), the
#                expression fingerprint (the digest of the canonical
#                clause text), the canonical_expression record (ContractExprIR
#                — op words + canonical texts; constants by value,
#                operators by kind; the message and spans never ride the
#                identity) and the declared message (None when none).
#   tests      — TEST DISCOVERY (audit item 19): one TestRelationship row
#                per EXERCISED DEF of a DISCOVERED test. Discovery = the
#                @test-marked function items of the finalized typed
#                program — the SAME marker the driver's test discovery
#                reads (attr.name == "test" on the item's attribute list,
#                driver.tg's run_test_files); the parser's `test "name" do`
#                sugar (parser.tg's test-block lowering) attaches NO
#                attribute, so sugar-only defs are never discovery rows
#                (they are invisible to the driver too — documented
#                compiler behavior, mirrored here). test = the test def's
#                StableDefId (span = None — provenance is never
#                serialized); target = each DEF-KEYED callee of the test's
#                LOWERED body, resolved through the item-10 call-site
#                machinery (the SAME caller->callee resolution the call
#                table rows ride: MirFnItem instance DefIds, the
#                def-emission-name join, the intrinsic-name family
#                excluded — an intrinsic site has no def key); one row per
#                (test, target), deduped. A discovered test with NO
#                lowered body (not compiled into the verified program) has
#                no call sites: the record's target is MANDATORY, so no
#                row can materialize an "empty target list" — the test is
#                then absent from the table, exactly as the model's own
#                doc states ("a test that exercises nothing never
#                appears"); a target-optional discovery row would be a
#                semantic_model.tg record change (out of scope here —
#                reported).
#   coverage   — EMPTY in a BUILD snapshot (the builder emits none); the
#                third-audit item-34 INGEST is the ONLY writer:
#                coverage_graph.tg's coverage_ingest reads a
#                tg.cov.trace.v1 trace (the runtime hook's output — see
#                that module's INSTRUMENTATION TARGET / TRACE FORMAT
#                sections) and populates one CoverageRelationship row per
#                reached tg.cov.v1 point: function = the point owner's
#                StableDefId, branch_id = the point's stable id text
#                (block id "<fn key>#B<ordinal>", edge id
#                "<from>|><to>|<kind>", StableContractId key, or effect-site
#                id "<fn key>|effect@<role>#<seq>"), arm_id = None
#                (block/edge coverage is not arm-granular), kind =
#                "Block" | "Edge" | "Contract" | "EffectSite", test_id =
#                the exercising test function's stable key text (the
#                model-side TEST ENDPOINT the item-19 follow-up added —
#                the defaulted "" is the unbound form, for facts recorded
#                outside a test run), span = None (the tg.cov.v1 ids are
#                span-free by construction). The §62 ordinal-scheme ids of
#                coverage.tg remain the CQS artifact domain — the snapshot
#                rows and the §40 indexes key on the tg.cov.v1 stable-id
#                grammar, never on dense ordinals re-derived at read time.
#                Evaluated-contract evidence
#                rides the snapshot's contracts table (keyed by
#                StableContractId), NOT the coverage table.
#   mir_functions — one semantic summary row per LOWERED FUNCTION of the
#                verified MIR — def-keyed AND synthesized (item 12; the
#                rows replace the old def-only table): block/statement/
#                local counts, reachability (the verified program IS the
#                reachable program), the calls_unsafe / calls_unknown
#                fail-closed markers and the transitive §11 effect
#                summary. Every row is keyed by its ORIGIN's canonical
#                text (the MirOrigin grammar below): def-keyed functions
#                keep their def digest key; instances ride the emission/
#                instance key; closures, drop glue, effect dispatchers and
#                extern shims ride the origin words + their program texts —
#                the same canonical texts the later delta/index consumers
#                key on. All rows participate in the effect propagation
#                graph (documented).
#   public_api_hash — digest of the sorted pub rows (symbols + types) with
#                their canonical signature-carrying keys.
#   abi_hash    — digest of the sorted ABI rows: pub top-level non-generic
#                Function defs whose def-keyed lowered function is in the
#                verified program, rendered with the mono.tg ABI
#                classifier's canonical frame (type_canon_render
#                CanonExternal + the stable-path map — the type encoding
#                the TANGERINE_ABI mangling digests). Generic bases render
#                a deterministic marker; a signature the External frame
#                rejects renders the fail-closed marker. Pointer widths
#                are target-desc data and ride the header target text.
#   unsafe_hash — digest of the sorted unsafe rows: per def-keyed lowered
#                function, the unsafe-surface markers of its verified
#                body (the unsafe-fn marker, extern calls, transmutes,
#                unknown calls, and the transitive may_unsafe class).
#   unsafe_facts — the unsafe-surface FACT TABLE (audit item 16): one row
#                per unsafe marker the scan records on a def-keyed
#                lowering (the "unsafe-fn" / "extern-call:<name>" /
#                "transmute" / "unknown-call:<name>" marker words — the
#                SAME marker domain snapshot_unsafe_text renders; rows
#                for synthesized bodies and the transitive-unsafe class
#                word stay out by design, exactly as the hash domain
#                documents), mapped to (UnsafeKind, site): function key =
#                the def digest key text, kind = UnsafeFunction /
#                ExternBoundary / Transmute / UnknownUnsafeCall, site =
#                the marker's callee name ("" for the site-less
#                families), digest words = the stable digest of the fact's
#                canonical text. Deduped per (function, kind, site) and
#                sorted through semantic_unsafe_facts_sort.
#   abi_surfaces — the PERSISTED ABI/layout rows (audit item 18;
#                third-audit items 42/43): one row per pub def-keyed
#                function AND per pub extern declaration (the FFI boundary
#                surface: per-param class/location/extension renders from
#                the ONE plan authority classify_call_plan, the typed
#                access conventions, the owning/Copy return word, the
#                nullability rows, the variadic flag, the platform triple,
#                the failure convention and the enum-crossing boundary)
#                and per declared nominal type (layout size/alignment and
#                the "name offset size" field rows from
#                layout_of_concrete); unclassifiable surfaces persist an
#                "abi-fail-closed" row with its reason, never fabricated
#                values. Sorted through semantic_abi_surfaces_sort and
#                serialized after the unsafe-fact rows; the table rides
#                the snapshot digest preimage (revision), while abi_hash
#                stays the §30 CanonExternal text digest.
#   dependencies — the PERSISTED typed dependency graph (third-audit item
#                18): the per-family edge rows (TypeUse / TraitImpl /
#                TraitSelection / GenericInstantiation / LayoutDependency /
#                ConstEvalDependency / DerivedBody / ContractReference /
#                AbiDependency) emitted from TYPED finalized state by the
#                producer section below — resolved signatures and typed
#                field shapes, ImplInfo records, solved InstanceId
#                constants, MirStaticRef operands, derived-body lowerings
#                and typed ABI-surface references; NO producer parses a
#                rendered canonical string. Effect/capability propagation,
#                Call, TestReferences and Coverage keep their existing row
#                sources. The graph ALSO persists dependency_completeness
#                (fourth-audit P0-9): the per-RELATION-FAMILY producer
#                status table ("complete" / "partial" / "unavailable") the
#                builder stamps from this section's documented producer
#                coverage, so the affected closure can tell a legitimately
#                empty family (Complete-no-dependents) from a family whose
#                dependents are unknown and must be reported, never
#                substituted by the call closure. Sorted through
#                semantic_dependency_graph_sort and serialized after the
#                ABI-surface rows; the graph rides the snapshot digest
#                preimage (revision).
#
# STABLE IDENTITY: every def's StableDefId is rooted on its PERSISTENT
# DECLARATION LINEAGE (third-audit item 11; fourth-audit P0-1: the identity
# digests (package, lineage, kind) ONLY — the current module path, the
# declared name and the signature are revision metadata/fingerprints). The
# def walk stamps each declaration through the threaded DeclLineageStore
# (stable_decl_stamp — an existing structural key keeps its number;
# stable_decl_stamp_renamed — a unique same-kind/same-signature entry seen
# in the immediately preceding revision transfers its number; explicit
# DeclContinuations take precedence) and builds the row id with
# stable_def_id_of_decl, so the StableDefId DIGEST WORDS are the
# StableDeclId's: a rename, a MOVE between modules or a nearby insertion
# leaves the declaration's artifact identity byte-identical, and a
# signature edit is the same declaration with a changed key text. The
# canonical "path::name#signature" key text still rides every row (resolver
# registration key + the signature text below) for rendering and boundary
# parsing; the text-derived stable_def_id_digested route remains only for
# synthesized/intrinsic rows with no declared lineage. A
# whitespace/comment-only edit reproduces every table and every digest
# byte-for-byte.
#
# HARD-FAILURE POLICY (audit item 8): no canonical text below falls back to
# a per-compilation-id render. Every renderer that could degrade an
# identity to a dense id ("Named#" + TypeId, "f<index>", "v<index>",
# "l<id>" for an out-of-range local) is Result-typed, and the builder
# (semantic_snapshot_of_final_state) fails with the SnapshotError variants
# instead. Per-snapshot DENSE LOCATORS that remain by explicit design
# (documented at each site): effect ids render as their interned ids
# ("e<id>" — the §11 EffectId domain of the producing env), generic
# parameters render as (index, owner-numeric), MIR local ordinals render
# for UNNAMED locals inside canonical place keys ("l<id>" — the lowered
# program's own slot identity, reproducible byte-for-byte from the same
# source), and capability ids render as their fixed §11 band. None of
# these is ever substituted for a missing stable identity.
#
# SITE-FIELD POLICY (audit item 47 — locators vs revision-stable node
# identity): the §33 "<caller key>#B<block id>#T" site texts the rows
# below carry (the INDIRECT-call rows' site — the only snapshot row
# family whose site IS a MIR node) are DENSE WITHIN-SNAPSHOT LOCATORS
# (SnapshotMirLocator, stable_ids.tg section 8): the block/statement
# ordinals are positions in THIS compilation's lowering, so one unrelated
# insertion mid-block renumbers the whole tail of the "#S"/"#T" node
# domain of that block. They stay locators here BY DESIGN — a row's site
# field is a reference INTO the same revision's own MIR, and the
# statement-level node rows of the §33 slice domain (MirSlice /
# SliceResult statement lists) use the same locator key texts. The
# REVISION-STABLE identity of the node behind any of these locator texts
# is CONTENT-derived — StableSemanticNodeId — by the SLICE LAYER
# (semantic_slice.tg's stable_node_id_of / stable_node_ids_of_slice,
# audit item 47), never re-derived inside this builder: no snapshot
# change is needed while the site fields stay locators. The summary rows
# (MirSemanticSummary) carry no site text at all (per-function structural
# counts only); the call/ownership/effect/contract row spans are
# presentation metadata and the ownership rows' place_key names a place,
# never a node. The coverage rows' branch/arm keys embed block/terminator
# ordinals — the §62 coverage domain's own dense grammar, outside the §33
# statement-node domain — and stay unchanged here.
#
# DETERMINISM: every emission table is sorted through the semantic_model.tg
# sorts (stable-digest order) before any rendering or hashing. All Map/Set
# uses below are index construction, fixed-point joins or sorted-key
# materializations — order-insensitive by construction; the only Map
# iteration that reaches text is the module_symbols keys materialized into
# a Vec and SORTED before any rendering.

use std::collections::{Vec, Map, Set}

